-- CK-269: a value that fills a deep tuple has a summary as large as the program (#856).
-- `w5`'s result is a tuple 16 levels deep that holds `x` at 2^16 places.
-- Without the path cut (§16.7 (c)) its summary lists every place, so
-- `--ownership-everywhere` stops at the `entries` limit: 1 276 786 entries.
-- The fix is a summary form that shares identical sub-summaries, not a cap.
-- Golden: no limit line and no demand; the slice that turns it green
-- blesses the summary lines it then prints.
w1 x = ( x, x )


w2 x = w1 (w1 x)


w3 x = w2 (w2 x)


w4 x = w3 (w3 x)


pub w5 x = w4 (w4 x)
